From a212b02f1999f4548aa85f87c55509746bc2ef73 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charlie Shao <charlie.shao@nordicsemi.no>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 13:20:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(zephyr): close HTTP/TLS socket on upload failure in
 memfault_zephyr_port_post_data

memfault_zephyr_port_post_data() only called
memfault_zephyr_port_http_close_socket() when the whole operation
succeeded (rv == 0). If memfault_zephyr_port_http_open_socket()
succeeded but memfault_zephyr_port_http_upload_sdk_data() then failed
(e.g. an HTTP response timeout after the TLS handshake had already
completed), the socket fd and its mbedTLS heap allocations were never
freed. ctx is stack-local, so the leak is permanent for the life of
the device, not just until the next successful sync.

Observed in the field via Memfault: ncs_mbedtls_heap_used jumped and
got stuck at 2x baseline for 5+ hours immediately after a
sync_memfault_failure event, until a later, unrelated Assert in the
tcp_work thread rebooted the device and reset the heap back to
baseline. Root-caused by symptom: a stack-overflow-shaped assert with
no actual stack depletion, caused instead by heap corruption from the
leaked/never-freed allocation.

Fixed upstream in memfault-firmware-sdk v1.27.0:
https://github.com/memfault/memfault-firmware-sdk/pull/92
This NCS v2.6.4 tree vendors v1.6.0, which predates that fix.
---
 ports/zephyr/common/memfault_platform_http.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ports/zephyr/common/memfault_platform_http.c b/ports/zephyr/common/memfault_platform_http.c
index 0442eeb..4e30692 100644
--- a/ports/zephyr/common/memfault_platform_http.c
+++ b/ports/zephyr/common/memfault_platform_http.c
@@ -614,9 +614,12 @@ int memfault_zephyr_port_post_data(void) {
     rv = memfault_zephyr_port_http_upload_sdk_data(&ctx);
   }
 
-  if (rv == 0) {
-    memfault_zephyr_port_http_close_socket(&ctx);
-  }
+  // Always close the socket, even on failure: memfault_zephyr_port_http_upload_sdk_data()
+  // can fail after the TLS handshake has already completed (e.g. a response timeout),
+  // and ctx is stack-local here, so skipping this on failure leaks the fd and its
+  // mbedTLS heap allocations for the life of the device. Fixed upstream in
+  // memfault-firmware-sdk v1.27.0 (https://github.com/memfault/memfault-firmware-sdk/pull/92).
+  memfault_zephyr_port_http_close_socket(&ctx);
 
 #if defined(CONFIG_MEMFAULT_SYNC_MEMFAULT_METRICS)
   if (rv == 0) {
-- 
2.50.1 (Apple Git-155)

